 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Just got a new Siemens dishwasher and there's always a bit of water left in the bottom under the filter after it finishes. Is it draining properly?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "A small amount of water remaining in the sump (under the filter) after a cycle finishes is actually normal. This residual water keeps the pump seals lubricated and prevents odours from rising up the drain pipe. If the water there is clear, it is likely just the normal seal-wetting level. If the water is murky, soapy, or smells like dirty wash water, that indicates a partial blockage in the filter or sump area preventing full drainage."
  }
 ],
